WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 003, en. Timings estimated from the script until the clip is rendered (re-split 27 Oct 2026: <=2x42 chars, <=20 cps, <=180 wpm).

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
<v Nia>Bore da. Same hill,
a few hundred years on.

2
00:00:03.278 --> 00:00:06.787
<v Nia>Who was farming it,
and what was on their minds?

3
00:00:15.207 --> 00:00:17.340
<v a Romano-British farmer>[in Welsh] Good spelt this year.

4
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.320
<v a Romano-British farmer>Dry enough to thresh before
the rain comes up the valley.

5
00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:26.140
<v a Romano-British farm woman>Then thresh it quick. The quern's
hungry, and so are the children.

6
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.026
<v a Romano-British farmer>The soldiers' buyers are
at the river ford tomorrow.

7
00:00:30.146 --> 00:00:34.006
<v a Romano-British farmer>They pay for the grain in
salt and good red pots.

8
00:00:34.426 --> 00:00:39.338
<v a Romano-British farm woman>Pots from far away, and we still
eat the same porridge out of them.

9
00:00:39.758 --> 00:00:44.320
<v a Romano-British farmer>Mam's mother used to say her people
kept a round house right here.

10
00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.896
<v a Romano-British farmer>Now it's the barn and the oxen.

11
00:00:47.316 --> 00:00:50.825
<v a Romano-British farm woman>Call them in. There's cloud
coming up off the marsh.

12
00:00:51.245 --> 00:00:55.806
<v a Romano-British farm woman>The geese are fat this year.
One for the turn of the year.

13
00:00:56.226 --> 00:01:00.787
<v a Romano-British farmer>And one for your mother,
or we'll never hear the end of it.

14
00:01:01.207 --> 00:01:05.067
<v a Romano-British farmer>Let them run. The hill's
big enough for all of us.

15
00:01:05.487 --> 00:01:10.620
<v Nia>That's a picture built from what the
digs found on this hill: grain, pottery,

16
00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:15.653
<v Nia>people at work. The digs keep their
own dates, and we'll read them there.

17
00:01:16.073 --> 00:01:17.373
<v The Grandson>And their names?

18
00:01:17.793 --> 00:01:20.951
<v Nia>Not one, yet. Next,
the graves by the church.
